  body = "Keep small TCG invalidation page-lock sets in four caller-owned sorted\nentries. Create the tree only on the fifth distinct existing page and\ntransfer held and busy state into stable heap entries without releasing\nlocks. Retain discovery acquisition order, ascending retry and release,\nopposite-page deduplication, and precise-SMC cleanup before nonlocal exit.\n\nRetain versioned process control, exact virtual coordinates, independent\nchild resources, canonical guest-state projection and complete matching\nsource integration. Preserve stopped-owner generations, registered reader\nand callback custody, FIFO barriers, fault settlement and descriptor\nfailure refusal across snapshot, restore and retained fork operations.\n\nPreserve accelerator instance classification, cold continuation checks,\nempty fault-queue admission, active instruction-context observation,\ndirect register-rule presence, cached tick-mode admission and native\nmutex owner identity. Keep tracked waiter updates under the existing\nregistry guard, with unsigned wrap, underflow refusal, condition waiter\nidentity and retained fork transaction ordering unchanged.\n\nKeep ordinary RR event ordering and Sim flush fixed points. Preserve all\nguest accesses, invalidation ranges, PageDesc and TB membership, dirty\naccounting, callback order, replay clock observations and scheduling.\n\nExercise actual page collection, native fast invalidation, locked range\nhandling and native page removal with explicit providers. Compare exact\nbaseline lock traces for zero, missing, duplicate, boundary and spilled\nsets, including busy trylocks and precise-SMC nonlocal cleanup. Carry\ncausal controls for omitted pages, lost spill state, missing cleanup,\nreversed iteration, absent first-page admission and eager tree creation.\n\nExtend the system-mode x86 SMC regression with a shared first physical\npage and five distinct second pages, patches through both memberships,\nspilled current-TB cleanup and restored temporary mappings. Retain the\nstrict public prototypes and compiler macros in the native waiter proof.\n\nStrict source-built syntax checks pass for the prototype, baseline and\nall six mutations. The inline collection remains a prototype pending\nconfigured native execution, guest, replay and performance qualification.\n\nKeep a page-locked derived count of recorded TB memberships requiring a\nsecond distinct physical page. Skip only the preliminary lock-discovery\nwalk when that count is zero after acquiring the page lock. Preserve\nnonzero and unknown traversal, retry ordering and actual invalidation.\nSaturate at UINT32_MAX, retain unknown until the list is empty or fully\ncleared, and update only insertion, successful tagged unlink and full flush.\nKeep physical aliases at zero and invalid retained memberships counted.\n\nExtract native insertion, duplicate-QHT rollback, hash invalidation and\nrecursive list-clear bodies into focused proofs. Verify both list tags,\nmixed lists, final crossing removal, sticky saturation, empty and flush\nrecovery, retry after a competing membership change, precise-SMC cleanup\nand retained process fork copies. Strict source-built compilation and\nexecution pass. Seven causal controls fail runtime native assertions;\nsealed-baseline collection stdout matches exactly. Guest SMC, MTTCG,\nreplay and performance remain unqualified for this prototype.\n\nPlace the crossing count directly after QemuSpin, before the tagged list\nhead. The extracted native QemuSpin and PageDesc definitions measured with\nthe source-built 64-bit compiler retain the baseline 16-byte descriptor,\nusing the existing four-byte padding rather than enlarging it to 24 bytes.\nThis layout probe is not a full configured QEMU compilation. The same nine\nfocused proof cases pass after the layout correction.\n\nRetain a thread-private validated search position for x86 TSC sources.\nResolve it against current array storage and compare the complete source\nkind and instance on every hit; keep original scans for misses and all\nother clock kinds. Remain useful before binding or manifest finalization\nwithout caching pointers, absent results, activation, values or time.\nPreserve live guards, transform evidence, replay and clock-read ordering.\n\nExercise production lookup, manifest sorting, activation and projection\nbodies with real GLib arrays, native fork and a cold replacement thread.\nCompare sealed-reference traces and quiescent relocation, sorting, exact\nkeys, live restore guards, values and terminal refusal. Nine compiled\ncausal controls fail native assertions. Preserve the existing exhaustive\ncold fault proof with the original clock-kind enum in its test adapter.\nRegistry mutation providers remain quiescent; guest, migration-stream,\nretained-runtime and performance qualification remain outstanding.\n\nEmit the native unsealed second-lookup row count on stderr after its\nassertion. Retain five identical lifecycle stdout observations and all\nproduction functions. Strict proofs retain candidate one-row lookup,\nreference five-row lookup and nine native assertion controls.\n\nAdd opt-in native node command and stop callbacks on the GPL-side plugin\ninterface. Preserve legacy dispatch when no native control is registered.\nBind immutable command sequences and digests; refuse settlement and nonzero\nphase or microstep requests rather than substituting legacy execution.\n\nClamp RR retirement to an exclusive native ceiling using absolute 50 ps\ninstruction service. Administrative parks retain the next retirement deadline\nand partial service credit across command partitions without rebasing time.\nKeep virtual timers, including AioContext lists, behind the native RR owner;\nwithhold modeled work while no command is admitted or after a stop receipt.\n\nExtend the resource manifest with the V4 native control descriptor, callback,\nworker and prepared-scope identity. Validate the connected Unix datagram fd\nand retain its device/inode identity. Keep native inventory incomplete and\nrefuse capture, restore and hot fork while command-journal custody remains\nunqualified; reject legacy time advancement under native registration.\n\nCarry service-clock VMState scalars and hostile-state validation without\nclaiming complete native state support. Stop receipts expose native deadlines\nand service credit with unknown pending-source inventory. Idle transitions,\ndevice/input/output closure, settlement and full native profiles remain\nunsupported. Add arithmetic and real-QEMU ceiling and partition fixtures.\n\nDiagnostic source builds for x86_64 and aarch64 and actual x86 exclusive-ceiling\nand partition probes passed. Their binaries retain the old package identity;\nthese diagnostics establish neither packaged qualification nor distribution.\n\nRetain original PIT timer arms with native generations, FIFO order and\nexclusive timing horizons. Emit scoped CPU park and timer facts without\nclaiming complete interrupt, deferred-work, input or device closure. Preserve\nthe next service deadline and genuine original timer arms across partitions.\n\nAdd private KVM clock component negotiation and QMP control while refusing\nunsupported acceleration and unqualified complete node profiles. Native\nx86_64 and aarch64 source builds and existing Aio, icount and vCPU service\nregressions pass; live x86 CPU/timer probes preserve original custody.\nThis component stage does not qualify complete native capture or forks.\n\nRetain a genuine asynchronous native writer HOLD through the original\nRR owner instead of permitting broad event-loop release. The held query\nbinds scope, original command, generation and bounded native CPU, work,\nBH, Aio and handler inventories. A wrong scope or insufficient capacity\nrefuses without releasing or replacing original writer custody.\n\nKeep pointer-bearing native rows local to the GPL process; portable\nobservations contain only checked scalar identities and process-neutral\ncoordinates. Preserve legacy execution when native control is disabled.\n\nNative x86 and ARM builds, 33 Aio tests, icount/service regressions and\nexclusive CPU/PIT partition probes pass. CPU/IRQ future producers,\nplugin journals, input/output payloads and complete device state remain\nunqualified; this stage does not enable native capture or fork.\n\nRetain the first unknown native CPU-work, interrupt or reset source diagnostic under the original prepared scope. Preserve actual queued work and expose immutable unknown-birth/effects facts without waiting for BQL or claiming physical containment. Invalidate fresh execution and stop evidence after the source fault; require independent supervisor containment. Bound original native run-owner scalar history.\n\nAdd opt-in original construction epochs and bounded native HOME processing\nunder the pinned initialization scope. Retain original pending callbacks,\nwriter generations and immutable cuts until matching acknowledgement. Keep\nordinary execution closed before acknowledgement and preserve the existing\nV4 command, FIFO and absolute instruction-service semantics.\n\nAdd separately negotiated KVM kernel edition three with its exact component\nbitmap and disjoint QMP namespace. Retain edition one behavior and refuse\nunsupported acceleration, device absence and complete profile qualification.\nKeep the userspace exit, device/input and whole-domain closure gaps explicit.\n\nPreserve the production CPU reset-ingress guard while providing its existing\nno-CPU unit link target with a queue-checked stub. No native source file is\nadded or removed, and every original source license remains unchanged.\n\nCombined x86_64 and aarch64 configured default builds pass, together with\n46 native unit cases, both initial-argument refusal suites, actual KVM\ncomponent refusal cases and extracted-production ABI/error checks. The\nactual host/plugin/native initialization probe and four V4 native control\nregressions pass against the combined sources. These component results do\nnot qualify complete native readiness, phase/input closure, snapshots,\nretained forks, or actual KVM execution on a host lacking the device.";
